/* book exam traps: Do not swap QH and QC: QH is the larger heat flow to the hot side, QC is the smaller flow from the cold side, and W is their difference. | COP is not W/QC. It is QC/W for a refrigerator and QH/W for a heat pump. | For a refrigerator or heat pump, work input W is positive in the magnitude balance QH = QC + W. Do not enter it as negative and then add signs again. | A heat pump and a refrigerator are the same device with a different wanted output; COPHP = COPR + 1, not a separate cycle. | η and COP are ratios of energies, so no temperature enters them. Temperatures appear only in the Carnot limits, and there they must be in kelvin. */
